# Executive Summary

## Due Oct 25, 2026

=== layout: one-panel

# Executive Summary

@body

- A [one-page proposal]{color=red} that can stand on its own.
- Connect the problem, biological mechanism, and product.
- Identify customers, competition, and development milestones.
- Support important claims with sources.
- Write the summary after planning the full argument.

=== layout: one-panel

# Executive Summary: Submission

@body

- Submit through Blackboard.
- [Three-page limit]{color=red}: cover, one-page summary, references.
- The summary itself must fit on one page.
- Check the uploaded format after Turnitin processes the file.
- [Similarity scores above 10% lose points.]{color=red}
- Select your topic and address the feedback; approval is not required.

=== layout: one-panel

# Three-Page Executive Summary

@body

| Page | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| 1: Cover | Company name, logo, optional table of contents |
| 2: Summary | One page after upload; similarity above 10% loses points |
| 3: References | Sources for the facts and claims |

=== layout: one-panel

# Use the samples as writing case studies

@body

- Notice how the writer connects problem, product, science, and market.
- Check what the cited research actually demonstrates.
- Look for the customer, alternatives, and next measurable milestone.
- Old sample claims and dates need fresh evidence.
- Lecture 06D works through examples from the sample collection.

=== layout: one-panel

# Executive Summary Rubric

@body

| Criterion | Weight | Look for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Cover | 10% | Effective company name; clean cover |
| Problem | 15% | Clear statement of the problem |
| Background | 15% | Context and scientific basis |
| Solution | 15% | Product and how it solves the problem |
| Business model | 15% | Market need and product niche |
| Enthusiasm | 15% | Belief in the product; engaging writing |
| Style | 15% | Readable fonts, spacing, and justified text |

=== layout: one-panel

# Most Common Errors

@body

- Similarity scores above 10% will lose points
- Executive summary does not hit all major areas\:
  - Background, Problem, Solution, Scientific Basis, Business Model, Competition
    - I am not concerned about the order, but it needs to make sense
- Background portion does not provide any background information

